                                                                            <comments>
                            <comment id="370412" author="adilger" created="Tue, 25 Apr 2023 00:33:28 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;The sanity.sh test_119d subtest is removed via patch &lt;a href=&quot;https://review.whamcloud.com/50731&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;https://review.whamcloud.com/50731&lt;/a&gt; &quot;&lt;tt&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-13706&quot; title=&quot;sanity test_119d: the read rpcs have not completed in 2s&quot; class=&quot;issue-link&quot; data-issue-key=&quot;LU-13706&quot;&gt;&lt;del&gt;LU-13706&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt; tests: remove test 119d&lt;/tt&gt;&quot;.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="425382" author="adilger" created="Thu, 22 Aug 2024 00:36:01 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;It looks like patch &lt;a href=&quot;https://review.whamcloud.com/56113&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;https://review.whamcloud.com/56113&lt;/a&gt; &quot;&lt;tt&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-12567&quot; title=&quot;ha-all-ior-ssf-fpp-mdtest: IOR fpp: cannot close file. ERROR: Input/output error&quot; class=&quot;issue-link&quot; data-issue-key=&quot;LU-12567&quot;&gt;&lt;del&gt;LU-12567&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt; ptlrpc: handle reply and resend reorder&lt;/tt&gt;&quot; is fixing sanity.sh test_224 which was setting &lt;tt&gt;fail_loc=OBD_FAIL_PTLRPC_CLIENT_BULK_CB=0x515&lt;/tt&gt; on the client and checking it in the OST target code. &lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="425383" author="adilger" created="Thu, 22 Aug 2024 00:39:53 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;There are also several other OBD_FAIL cases listed in &lt;a href=&quot;https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-10363&quot; title=&quot;some fail_locs set on client but checked on server&quot; class=&quot;issue-link&quot; data-issue-key=&quot;LU-10363&quot;&gt;LU-10363&lt;/a&gt; that are set on the client and checked on the server, but I haven&apos;t looked if they overlap with the test cases here. &lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="499653" author="adilger" created="Fri, 14 Aug 2026 21:03:12 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Alex not working on this, but it would be good for a new developer.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="499654" author="adilger" created="Fri, 14 Aug 2026 21:08:44 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;It would be good to update patch &lt;a href=&quot;https://review.whamcloud.com/50240&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;https://review.whamcloud.com/50240&lt;/a&gt; (&quot;&lt;a href=&quot;https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-16636&quot; title=&quot;some tests don&apos;t hit fail_loc&quot; class=&quot;issue-link&quot; data-issue-key=&quot;LU-16636&quot;&gt;LU-16636&lt;/a&gt; tests: catch unused fail_loc&quot;) to land to master, so that it can catch new subtests that are adding fail_loc and not hitting it, or regress because of a code change.  It should add a specific list of &quot;known broken&quot; subtests (hopefully not longer than the list above) and use `error_ignore &lt;a href=&quot;https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-16636&quot; title=&quot;some tests don&apos;t hit fail_loc&quot; class=&quot;issue-link&quot; data-issue-key=&quot;LU-16636&quot;&gt;LU-16636&lt;/a&gt;` for those, otherwise trigger a real `error` if the subtest is failing.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;It may be that we also have some racy subtests that do not hit the `fail_loc` 100% of the time.  Ideally those tests would run longer or loop to ensure the issue is hit on each run, but that may not always be practical and they would need to be excepted for now.  I can&apos;t think of a way for &lt;tt&gt;test-framework.sh&lt;/tt&gt; to track the hit rate over time to determine if the percentage of hits changes (which may also be conditional on the runtime environment, etc). &lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="499711" author="gerrit" created="Mon, 17 Aug 2026 12:53:54 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;&quot;Alex Zhuravlev &amp;lt;bzzz@whamcloud.com&amp;gt;&quot; uploaded a new patch: &lt;a href=&quot;https://review.whamcloud.com/c/fs/lustre-release/+/68044&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;https://review.whamcloud.com/c/fs/lustre-release/+/68044&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br/&gt;
